Subject: Re: Integration follow-up: model routing & policy configuration — sample policy + SDK snippet

Hi Sam / Priya — attaching the sample routing policy and a short SDK + auth snippet for your engineering team to try. High-level notes inline below and a proposed 30-min tech sync on Tue 3/16 at 10am PT (same as proposed) — please confirm.

Attached: proposed-routing-policy.yaml (example), redwood-integration-mmap.pdf

Sample routing highlights (TL;DR):
- Route names: interactive-chat (latency-first), async-rerank (cost-first), embeddings-index (batch)
- Latency policy: interactive-chat SLO p90=200ms, p95=300ms. If p95 > 300ms for rolling 1m window -> escalate to fallback chain.
- Fallback chain (example): interactive-chat -> redwood-small-v1-quant (primary) -> redwood-medium-v1-quant (secondary) -> enqueue to async-rerank with cached prefix (tertiary).
- Region routing: policy supports per-request region tag (us/eu) and will pin to region-deployed variants. EU data path is configured to enforce EU-only endpoints; failure mode defaults to block unless explicit allow-failover flag is set.
- Auth & SDK: sample JS snippet below (also in the Drive link):

// Install: npm i @redwood/inference
import Redwood from '@redwood/inference';
const client = new Redwood({ apiKey: process.env.REDWOOD_API_KEY, region: 'us-west-2' });

// Example: call the interactive-chat route (latency-first)
const resp = await client.routes.call('interactive-chat', {
  input: 'Help me find shipment ETA for PO 12345',
  routing: { region: 'us', allowFailover: false },
  structured_output: { schema: 'shipment_slot_v1' }
});

// Embeddings + rerank pattern (pseudo):
// 1) compute cheap embeddings with small-embed-v1 for candidate retrieval
// 2) vector search in your index -> topK
// 3) call 'async-rerank' route for cross-encoder reranking of topK

Observability & billing: route-level cost and token breakdowns will show in Redwood Console. We'll share a short walkthrough in the tech sync.

Next steps: please confirm Tue 3/16 10am PT for the sync and share any other folks who should join (infra/security).

